==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From American seismologist [[w:Charles Richter|Charles Richter]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|En-us-Richter scale.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|head=[[Richter]] [[scale]]}}

# {{context|seismology|lang=en}} a [[logarithmic]] [[scale]] used to [[express]] the [[energy]] released by an [[earthquake]], each [[increase]] of 1 representing a 32-fold increase in energy.

